static const struct KakuNote U10N[] = {
	{ "Comparing two things", "AのほうがBより + adjective says A is more... than B. You can flip it to BよりAのほうが with no change in meaning. In an answer, のほうが alone is enough.", U10N0EX, 2 },
	{ "Comparing three or more", "With a whole group, use [group]でいちばん + adjective. The group can be a category (くだもので), a place (にほんで) or a list.", U10N1EX, 2 },
	{ "の standing in for a noun", "Once the noun is obvious, replace it with の: あかいの is \"the red one\". This is the same の you met in 〜のが好きです, doing the same job.", U10N2EX, 2 },
	{ "〜つもりです", "Short form plus つもりです states a firm intention — something you have decided, not a vague hope.", U10N3EX, 2 },
	{ "Adjective + なる", "なる means \"become\". い-adjectives change their ending to く (さむくなる), な-adjectives and nouns take に (げんきになる, せんせいになる).", U10N4EX, 2 },
	{ "どこかに and どこにも", "どこかに means \"(to) somewhere\", どこにも with a negative means \"(to) nowhere\". Matching pairs exist for なにか／なにも and だれか／だれも.", U10N5EX, 2 },
	{ "で for means of transport", "The same で that marks where an action happens also marks what you do it by: train, bus, bike. On foot is the exception — あるいて, the te-form of あるく.", U10N6EX, 2 },
};
