static const char* const C6B[] = { "When you want to add a second person or thing to something already said, you swap は for も. Not add — swap.", "はるとさんはにほんじんです。もりせんせいもにほんじんです。 The second sentence does not need to repeat the whole idea; も carries \"also is Japanese\" on its own.", "The reason it replaces は is that both are doing the same job — pointing at what the sentence is about. You cannot point twice." };
