static const char* const C10B[] = { "The ます form is called present tense, which is slightly misleading. It covers habits — things you do regularly — and things you are going to do. It does not cover the past.", "まいにちコーヒーをのみます is a habit. あしたコーヒーをのみます is tomorrow. Same verb form; the time word does the work.", "The negative is ません, and it behaves the same way: たべません is both \"I do not eat\" and \"I am not going to eat\"." };
