static const char* const C11B[] = { "Most of the frequency words are straightforward: よく often, ときどき sometimes, たいてい usually. They sit before the verb and that is that.", "But あまり and ぜんぜん are different. あまり means \"not much\" and ぜんぜん means \"not at all\" — the \"not\" is part of their meaning, so the verb has to be negative as well. あまりたべます is not a sentence.", "Think of them as needing a partner: the adverb sets up the negative and the verb delivers it." };
