static const char* const C13B[] = { "The time-of-day ones are simple enough: おはようございます in the morning, こんにちは through the day, こんばんは once it is dark. Dropping ございます makes it casual, for friends and family.", "The ones worth special attention are the pairs, because Japanese expects the other half. The person leaving says いってきます and the one staying answers いってらっしゃい. Coming home it is ただいま and おかえりなさい. Before eating いただきます, after it ごちそうさま.", "Learn each pair as one unit. Half a pair is a question with no answer." };
